 null, 'The Krebs cycle enzymes are located in the mitochondrial matrix, where the cycle oxidizes acetyl-CoA to generate NADH, FADH2, and ATP.'),
('NEET PG', 'Pre- and Para-Clinical Sciences', 'Biochemistry', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Which amino acid serves as the precursor for the synthesis of dopamine and norepinephrine?',
